{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xts8UExT9L25YMq5T8JwkM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Edge cases\n2\t\n3\t## Batch and day aliases\n4\t- \"cse a\", \"CSE A\", \"cse-a\" → `CSE-A`. The script normalises case, spaces and hyphens.\n5\t- \"mon\", \"Mon.\" → `Monday`; the script accepts 3-letter prefixes.\n6\t- \"today\" / \"tomorrow\": the script does not know the date. Ask the student which day they mean,\n7\t  or work it out from the session's current date if it is available, and **say which day you assumed**.\n8\t\n9\t## Weekends and holidays\n10\t- The CSV has no Saturday/Sunday rows. Answer \"no classes are scheduled\" rather than inventing any.\n11\t- The CSV has no holiday calendar. If asked \"is there class on <festival>?\", say the timetable\n12\t  does not cover holidays and point the student to the academic calendar.\n13\t\n14\t## Unknown batch or course\n15\t- Unknown batch (e.g. `MECH-A`): the script exits with code 2 and lists the valid batches.\n16\t  Show that list. Do not guess the closest batch.\n17\t- A course that is not in the CSV (e.g. \"Quantum Computing lab\"): say it is not in the timetable.\n18\t  Do not create rows, times or rooms for it. This is the main fabrication risk for this Skill.\n19\t\n20\t## Labs vs lectures\n21\t- `CS303` and `CS303L` are different rows. \"When is DBMS?\" should list both the lecture and the lab\n22\t  rows, labelled by `session_type`.\n23\t\n24\t## \"Next class\" / free-slot questions\n25\t- Sort the batch's rows for that day by `start`. A free slot is any gap between one row's `end`\n26\t  and the next row's `start`. Report gaps only within 09:00–17:00.\n27\t\n28\t## Conflicting or duplicated rows\n29\t- If two rows for the same batch overlap in time, report both and flag the clash. Do not pick one.\n30\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"868131be-0ec1-458a-a28b-7ea88b932c1b","uuid":"a5d58cb5-73c6-4db7-8768-8acf308ec1da","timestamp":"2026-11-18T08:43:06.953Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/cm/_69qrmd57sz5vxgbksyylrb00000gn/T/tmp0xb0skes/campus-helpdesk/skills/timetable-helper/references/edge-cases.md","content":"# Edge cases\n\n## Batch and day aliases\n- \"cse a\", \"CSE A\", \"cse-a\" → `CSE-A`. The script normalises case, spaces and hyphens.\n- \"mon\", \"Mon.\" → `Monday`; the script accepts 3-letter prefixes.\n- \"today\" / \"tomorrow\": the script does not know the date. Ask the student which day they mean,\n  or work it out from the session's current date if it is available, and **say which day you assumed**.\n\n## Weekends and holidays\n- The CSV has no Saturday/Sunday rows. Answer \"no classes are scheduled\" rather than inventing any.\n- The CSV has no holiday calendar. If asked \"is there class on <festival>?\", say the timetable\n  does not cover holidays and point the student to the academic calendar.\n\n## Unknown batch or course\n- Unknown batch (e.g. `MECH-A`): the script exits with code 2 and lists the valid batches.\n  Show that list. Do not guess the closest batch.\n- A course that is not in the CSV (e.g. \"Quantum Computing lab\"): say it is not in the timetable.\n  Do not create rows, times or rooms for it. This is the main fabrication risk for this Skill.\n\n## Labs vs lectures\n- `CS303` and `CS303L` are different rows. \"When is DBMS?\" should list both the lecture and the lab\n  rows, labelled by `session_type`.\n\n## \"Next class\" / free-slot questions\n- Sort the batch's rows for that day by `start`. A free slot is any gap between one row's `end`\n  and the next row's `start`. Report gaps only within 09:00–17:00.\n\n## Conflicting or duplicated rows\n- If two rows for the same batch overlap in time, report both and flag the clash. Do not pick one.\n","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":30}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Xts8UExT9L25YMq5T8JwkM","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
